00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.487
Scholarly.

66
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.032
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:52.288
Visal, what study skill has helped you the most this year?

68
00:03:53.383 --> 00:03:56.755
Active recall. I have improved my grades a lot.

69
00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:59.524
When did you start using it?

70
00:04:00.617 --> 00:04:05.057
I started last semester. I tested myself every night.

71
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.300
Have you tried spaced repetition too?

72
00:04:09.417 --> 00:04:14.333
Yes, I have used a flashcard app since March. It works!

73
00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:16.839
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:21.134
Grammar focus: Present perfect vs past simple.

75
00:04:21.434 --> 00:04:22.586
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:23.283 --> 00:04:24.900
I have improved my grades.

77
00:04:25.783 --> 00:04:27.887
I studied hard last semester.

78
00:04:28.783 --> 00:04:31.538
She has read three scholarly articles this week.

79
00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:39.483
Use the past simple with a finished time, like 'yesterday' or 'last semester'. Use the present perfect when the result matters now.

80
00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:44.158
Be careful! Don't say: I have studied hard last semester.

81
00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.564
Say: I studied hard last semester.

82
00:04:48.864 --> 00:04:52.059
Use the past simple with a finished time like 'last semester'.

83
00:04:52.867 --> 00:04:55.252
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:57.602
Smarter, Not Harder.

85
00:04:57.902 --> 00:05:01.480
Last year, I studied by re-reading my notes for hours.

86
00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.941
This year, I have switched to active recall and spaced repetition.

87
00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:09.537
As a result, my grades have improved a lot.

88
00:05:10.533 --> 00:05:14.402
I have also developed my research skills and learned to add a citation.

89
00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.932
Now I can analyze and evaluate evidence-based arguments.

90
00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:24.221
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:26.990
I blank hard last semester.

92
00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:30.897
A, studied. B, have studied. C, study.

93
00:05:34.433 --> 00:05:36.491
The answer is A: studied.

94
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.845
Testing yourself instead of re-reading is blank.

95
00:05:41.145 --> 00:05:45.437
A, active recall. B, a citation. C, an argument.

96
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.185
The answer is A: active recall.

97
00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.325
Being honest in your schoolwork is academic blank.

98
00:05:55.625 --> 00:05:59.325
A, integrity. B, argument. C, research.

99
00:06:02.867 --> 00:06:04.611
The answer is A: integrity.

100
00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.010
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:12.395
What study skill has helped you the most this year?

102
00:06:21.183 --> 00:06:22.591
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:22.891 --> 00:06:31.035
Spaced repetition has helped me the most. I started it in January, and I have learned over five hundred words since then.

104
00:06:31.335 --> 00:06:33.090
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:33.983 --> 00:06:38.807
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present perfect vs past simple.

106
00:06:39.107 --> 00:06:42.490
Today's value is hard work. Work hard and never give up.

107
00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.466
